2 CONT =====Wegelius=====
2 CONT https://fi.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wegelius The family descends in 1682? of the deceased farmer Tuomas Jaakonpoika from Uppa, who lived in Seinäjoki's Uppala house. Two of his six sons and the grandson of the third took a Latin-soundin
2 CONC g last name after going to school according to the custom of the time. The name was formed by translating the name of Seinäjoki into Swedish: Wäggälv, from which the surname was formed first Weggelfius, later Wegelius.[1] After th
2 CONC at, the family was known for a long time as a priest family.[2]
2 CONT
